# Brainrot.com — Motion System

Animation = brand personality, but **controlled**. Playful, tactile, responsive — never slow, corporate, or distracting.

## Durations

| Kind | Duration |
|---|---|
| Micro | 100–180ms |
| Button | 150–220ms |
| Card | 200–300ms |
| Page | 250–450ms |

Avoid long animations.

## Patterns

- **Hover cards**: slight scale + rotate + translateY + glow increase
- **Selection**: highlight selected; optionally dim others; animate product preview on switch — selection must stay clear **without** motion
- **Hero**: subtle float via CSS transforms (no JS animation loops)
- **Holo**: slow shared gradient motion; reuse CSS keyframes — don't animate every gradient independently

## Reduced motion

Always honor `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`:

- disable floating / large transforms
- shorten transitions
- keep state changes visually understandable

## Rule

Motion makes the site feel alive. It should never make it hard to use.

On the light canvas, prefer playful lift/tilt/gloss over heavy neon bloom.
No constant large movement, heavy parallax, or particle spam.
